WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.275
Welcome to Chart Plotting.

2
00:00:02.525 --> 00:00:05.350
This is the module you do with your hands.

3
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:07.850
No memorizing rhymes here.

4
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:14.900
You’ll draw lines on a real chart and measure them, and the exam checks whether your lines land in the right place.

5
00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:16.825
First, the kit.

6
00:00:17.075 --> 00:00:20.700
Parallel rulers, or a course plotter, for directions.

7
00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:23.550
A pair of dividers, for distances.

8
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:29.525
Sharp pencils, a good eraser, and a simple calculator if your exam allows one.

9
00:00:29.775 --> 00:00:31.625
And the chart itself.

10
00:00:31.875 --> 00:00:36.975
The exam is usually worked on NOAA training chart twelve ten T R.

11
00:00:37.225 --> 00:00:41.625
It covers Martha’s Vineyard to Block Island, up in New England.

12
00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:45.500
A Florida captain, tested on a Massachusetts chart?

13
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:47.900
Yes.

14
00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:51.325
Everyone in the country uses the same one.

15
00:00:51.575 --> 00:00:53.275
So buy it now.

16
00:00:53.525 --> 00:01:00.500
And practice with the very tools you’ll carry into the exam room, so your hands already know them on test day.
